From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kierandrewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mutter: keep the session when Xwayland exits

Mutter treats Xwayland as mandatory when the compositor does not run as a systemd user
unit, and it exits when Xwayland exits. Gnoblin runs under the display manager session
wrapper, so killing or crashing Xwayland ended the whole session and every Wayland app
with it.

Use the on-demand policy, as a GNOME Shell session does. Xwayland starts when the first
X11 client connects, and starts again after it exits.

---
diff --git a/src/core/meta-context-main.c b/src/core/meta-context-main.c
index e40394b368..36408aad1e 100644
--- a/src/core/meta-context-main.c
+++ b/src/core/meta-context-main.c
@@ -130,15 +130,17 @@ static MetaX11DisplayPolicy
 meta_context_main_get_x11_display_policy (MetaContext *context)
 {
   MetaContextMain *context_main = META_CONTEXT_MAIN (context);
-  g_autofree char *unit = NULL;
 
   if (context_main->options.no_x11)
     return META_X11_DISPLAY_POLICY_DISABLED;
 
-  if (sd_pid_get_user_unit (0, &unit) < 0)
-    return META_X11_DISPLAY_POLICY_MANDATORY;
-  else
-    return META_X11_DISPLAY_POLICY_ON_DEMAND;
+  /*
+   * Mutter makes Xwayland mandatory when it does not run as a systemd user
+   * unit, and exits when Xwayland exits. Gnoblin runs under the display
+   * manager's session wrapper, so any Xwayland crash ended the whole session.
+   * Start Xwayland on demand instead, and start it again after it exits.
+   */
+  return META_X11_DISPLAY_POLICY_ON_DEMAND;
 }
 
 static gboolean
